{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019vLPZ9QuNZ3h34MQFZMMGY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd092-mkfifo\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/mkfifo: Make FIFOs (Named Pipes)\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships mkfifo but the GNU version supports --mode (-m) for setting permissions\n6\t  at creation. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n7\t  (gmkfifo, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified\n8\t  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Create one or more named pipes (FIFOs).\n12\t  - G2: Support permission mode specification at creation.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gmkfifo via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: FIFO creation\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must create a FIFO (named pipe) at each specified path using the mkfifo(2) system call.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: Must process multiple NAME arguments, creating a FIFO for each.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the FIFO's permission bits to MODE (octal or symbolic). Default is 0666 modified by umask.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: Must exit 1 when any FIFO cannot be created (e.g., path already exists), printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining arguments.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: Must exit 0 when all FIFOs are created successfully.\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: Must exit 1 when any creation fails.\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n37\t\n38\tnon_goals:\n39\t  - cmd/mkfifo does not implement SELinux context setting.\n40\t\n41\tacceptance_criteria:\n42\t  - id: AC1\n43\t    criterion: \"mkfifo pipe1 creates a FIFO at pipe1, matching gmkfifo.\"\n44\t    traces:\n45\t      - R1.1\n46\t      - R1.2\n47\t  - id: AC2\n48\t    criterion: \"mkfifo -m 600 pipe1 creates a FIFO with mode 600, matching gmkfifo.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R1.3\n51\t  - id: AC3\n52\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gmkfifo passes for all required test cases.\"\n53\t    traces:\n54\t      - R1.1\n55\t      - R1.2\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t      - R1.4\n58\t  - id: AC4\n59\t    criterion: \"cmd/mkfifo compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R1.1\n62\t      - R1.2\n63\t      - R1.3\n64\t      - R1.4\n65\t      - R2.1\n66\t      - R2.2\n67\t      - R2.3\n68\t\n69\tpackage_contract:\n70\t  imports:\n71\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41a328ed-9f9c-4936-a3c8-d90e62e993de","uuid":"2d3468d8-5766-4e0d-880e-27cba738e133","timestamp":"2026-05-24T02:21:05.504Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5560/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd092-mkfifo.yaml","content":"id: srd092-mkfifo\ntitle: \"cmd/mkfifo: Make FIFOs (Named Pipes)\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships mkfifo but the GNU version supports --mode (-m) for setting permissions\n  at creation. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n  (gmkfifo, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified\n  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Create one or more named pipes (FIFOs).\n  - G2: Support permission mode specification at creation.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gmkfifo via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: FIFO creation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must create a FIFO (named pipe) at each specified path using the mkfifo(2) system call.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must process multiple NAME arguments, creating a FIFO for each.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the FIFO's permission bits to MODE (octal or symbolic). Default is 0666 modified by umask.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any FIFO cannot be created (e.g., path already exists), printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining arguments.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all FIFOs are created successfully.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any creation fails.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/mkfifo does not implement SELinux context setting.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"mkfifo pipe1 creates a FIFO at pipe1, matching gmkfifo.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"mkfifo -m 600 pipe1 creates a FIFO with mode 600, matching gmkfifo.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gmkfifo passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/mkfifo compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
